The '''Black Knights' Fortress''' is a castle of the [[Zamorakian]] military order of the [[Kinshra]], commonly referred to as the [[Black Knight|black knights]]. It plays a central role in the eponymous [[Black Knights' Fortress]] [[quest]], and is also visited during the [[King's Ransom]] and [[While Guthix Sleeps]] quests.

The interior and surrounding areas contain level 20 fortress guards and level 33 black knights. Unlike the guards, the knights are [[Aggressiveness|aggressive]] and will automatically attack lower-levelled players. The black knights in the meeting room with the large table will always be aggressive to players entering the room and disturbing their meeting.

An [[altar]] to Zamorak can be found on the {{FloorNumber|uk=1}}.

==History==
The fortress was constructed early in the [[Fifth Age]] back when the [[Kinshra]] were one of the groups who helped expand and defend the kingdom of [[Asgarnia]] under the rule of [[King Raddallin]].{{CiteText|text=Display case (Varrock Museum, number 4)}} The Kinshra have continued to use the fortress as a base since, where they now use it as part of their war against the [[White Knights]], who ousted them from power in [[Falador]] after [[King Vallance]] fell sick.{{CiteText|text=Display case (Varrock Museum, number 26)|quote=The old king of Asgarnia, King Vallance, falls very ill. The White Knights took advantage of this and began to take control of Falador and Asgarnia for themselves.}} The White Knights and Kinshra would clash in a [[Battle of North Falador|battle south of the fortress]],{{CiteText|text=Display case (Varrock Museum, number 33)|name = case|quote=Year 163, 5th Age - The White Knights declared that the Black knights were no longer to have any political power within Asgarnia. Lord Daquarius of the Kinshra immediately responds by declaring his Black Knights as being at a state of war with Falador. The two sides engaged in a big battle to the north of Falador.}} but as they were evenly matched, both sides retreated to build their forces and plot to wipe out the other side.{{CiteText|text=Display case (Varrock Museum, number 33)|quote=however, both sides were fairly evenly matched, and retreated to their fortresses to build up their forces and devise plans to crush the other, once and for all.}}
[[File:Black Knights' Fortress hall.png|thumb|none|The meeting hall and the witch's personal chamber.]]

==Transportation==
The Black Knights' Fortress can be reached a number of ways:
* Using the [[Arceuus spellbook]] spell [[Mind Altar Teleport]] and heading east.
* Using the [[Ancient Magicks]] spell [[Lassar Teleport]] and heading north.
* Using the [[standard spellbook]] spell [[Falador Teleport]] and heading north.
* Using the [[Construct. cape|Construction skillcape]] or [[Taverley teleport|Taverley teleport tablet]] to teleport to [[Taverley]] and heading east.
* Using the [[combat bracelet]] teleport to the [[Edgeville Monastery]] and heading around [[Ice Mountain]].
* Using the [[games necklace]] to the [[Burthorpe Games Room]] and heading south-east.

===Entering the fortress===
Players attempting to enter the fortress normally will be stopped from doing so by one of the [[Fortress Guard|fortress guards]]. In order to infiltrate the fortress, the player must be wearing one of the following combinations of armour:
*A [[bronze med helm]] and an [[iron chainbody]]
*A [[black full helm]], [[black platebody]], and [[black platelegs]]/[[black plateskirt]]
**[[Black trimmed armour]] and [[Black gold-trimmed armour]] also work, and can be mix and matched with regular Black armour
**[[Black heraldic armour]] does '''not''' work
*A set of [[elite black armour]]
*The [[Dark Squall robes]]

